Romhack Base: Majora's Mask
Timeline Placement: Not too long after Majora's Mask
Length: Short (4 Chapters)
Significance: Revisiting characters and places, as well as emotional closure

Synopsis:
[1] In this game, you play as the Deku Butler, who has learned somehow of the existence of Termina's Triforce, and intends to use its wish-granting ability to restore his son from his death-like state.
Unfortunately, someone else has grabbed the Triforce first, and due to their imbalanced heart, the 3 Pieces of the Triforce now abide with 3 troublesome individuals who are quite unwilling to hand them over.
An opening section in the Southern Swamp may be contrived: perhaps the Deku King says the Butler must do a thing before he is permitted to head out in search of the Triforce.

[2] The Triforce of Power is found first: in the hand of Mountain Smithy Zubora (the small guy). With power that has gone to his head, he now dresses like a king (though with consistently poor fashion sense).
He has abandoned the forge for a palace (much to Smithy Gabora's sadness and anger), and has pressed the gorons into being both palace servants and miners of precious metals for his pleasure.
Bring him to his senses to obtain the Triforce of Power!
2 new locations: Goron Mines and Zubora's Palace.

[3] The Triforce of Courage is located next: in the hand of Pirate Leader Aveil. With untempered courage, she commands her petty band of followers into dangerous waters in search of lost treasures.
Unfortunately her boldness stirs up monsters better left buried beneath the waves.
About 3 new locations: an archipelago full of holes where the pirates dug for treasure, a ship in transit where a battle with a sea monster takes place, and a mechanized lost city (Atlantis),
where the pirates uncover something terrifying (perhaps a dangerous version of the Romani Ranch aliens).
Aveil might not be fought at the end, but rather talked into handing over the Triforce after her underlings convince her it'd be for the best. However, the pirates themselves fight you once or twice as you follow their trail.

[4] The final part of the Triforce, the Triforce of Wisdom, remains with the one who first found and touched Termina's Triforce, causing it to split: the thief, Sakon.
Throughout the game, Sakon gains notoriety as he successfully steals more and more things... even some things of no particular value but that their owners cherished them.
At the Great Bay, the theft epidemic becomes noticable, though some might blame the pirates. After obtaining 2 Triforce Pieces, it becomes apparent that Sakon has become more than a mere menace around Termina.
He becomes such a threat that people from all regions band together to bring him down. Unfortunately for them, Sakon's hideout is impenetrable.
That is where you come in.
With 2 Triforce Pieces, you open the door... and find that his hideout has become a labyrinthine fortress of utmost cruelty and cunning.
Even with help from the other regions (Captain Viscen or grown-up Kafei? Zubora or Gabora or the Elder's Son? Romani? Aveil or the Beaver Brothers? Pamela? No one undead...
Various soldiers to be used as pawns on Sakon's oversized game boards?) this final location is gruelling to get through. And at the end of it all: Sakon puts on a powerful mask he found (not Majora's Mask) and attacks!
In the end, Sakon falls, and the Deku Butler gets his wish granted at last.

Items & Abilities:
Main tool: Butler's umbrella. Used for offense, defense, and traversal. Also can create wind?
Triforce Parts grant abilities. The Triforce of Power may grant fire resistance: that is, fire no longer kills the Butler with one touch.
The Triforce of Courage may grant some water specific ability: perhaps the ability to swim after bounces have been used up.
Other potential items: Empty Bottle, Mask of Scents, Candle, Magic Bubbles... Magic Belt (speed enhanced?)? Gold Dust Parasol?

